1
00:00:00,979 --> 00:00:04,269
- How else...?
- No, no, no.

2
00:00:04,691 --> 00:00:06,481
(Penny:)How else was I supposed to say it?

3
00:00:06,651 --> 00:00:11,151
(Leonard:)Slowly. Like putting a new fish in a tank.
You don't just drop it in.

4
00:00:11,323 --> 00:00:15,363
(Leonard:)You let the bag sit in the water
a while.

5
00:00:15,577 --> 00:00:17,657
(Sheldon:)The horror.

6
00:00:17,871 --> 00:00:21,371
- Sheldon, I'm sure it's gonna be fine.
- No, it's not going to be fine.

7
00:00:21,583 --> 00:00:25,333
(Sheldon:)Change is never fine.
They say it is, but it's not.

8
00:00:25,796 --> 00:00:28,376
Okay, did you even know the people
that are moving out?

9
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:29,840
(Sheldon:)I never met them.

10
00:00:30,008 --> 00:00:32,348
(Sheldon:)That's what made them perfect.

11
00:00:32,552 --> 00:00:34,512
(Sheldon:)There were no awkward hellos
in the halls.

12
00:00:34,679 --> 00:00:37,929
There's no clickety-clacking
of high-heel shoes on hardwood floors.

13
00:00:38,141 --> 00:00:42,941
(Sheldon:)They may as well have been a family of cats
just jumping around from drape to drape.

14
00:00:43,355 --> 00:00:46,605
And without that annoying
ammonia-urine smell.

15
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:50,240
(Penny:)I'm sure the new people
will be just as quiet.

16
00:00:50,445 --> 00:00:53,235
(Sheldon:)You can't know that.
How can you possibly know that?

17
00:00:53,448 --> 00:00:56,908
(Penny:)You're right, I can't. You know what?
Anyone could rent that apartment now.

18
00:00:57,119 --> 00:00:59,999
(Penny:)An opera singer, the cast of Stomp.

19
00:01:02,374 --> 00:01:05,214
(Penny:)Yeah, a tap-dancing pirate
with a wooden leg.

20
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:08,210
(Leonard:)Why are you making it worse?

21
00:01:08,421 --> 00:01:11,381
(Penny:)I tried making it better,
he wouldn't go for it.

22
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:12,590
[INAUDIBLE]

23
00:01:12,759 --> 00:01:14,889
- You're right. That's a great idea.
- What?

24
00:01:15,095 --> 00:01:18,095
(Howard:)I'll take the apartment.
I can finally get away from my mother...

25
00:01:18,306 --> 00:01:21,396
(Howard:)...and we can all spend
some more time together.

26
00:01:21,560 --> 00:01:23,810
(Howard:)If you catch my drift.

27
00:01:26,231 --> 00:01:29,031
(Sheldon:)The horror.

